{
  "meta": {
    "dialect": "Tokyo standard (東京式)",
    "notation": "accent = downstep position. 0 means no downstep (heiban). n>0 means pitch falls immediately after mora n.",
    "provenance": "Hand-curated, then checked entry by entry against English Wiktionary's Japanese pronunciation data. 37 of 37 remaining entries agree with Wiktionary. Two changes came out of that check: 居間 was corrected from heiban [0] to odaka [2], and the 二本/日本 pair was removed because 二本 has no Japanese section on Wiktionary and the kana page is a soft-redirect, so its accent could not be sourced from the reference this file cites. Several entries encode the accent as a letter (acc=h for heiban, acc=o for odaka) rather than a digit; those were resolved against the rendered page, since a digit search silently misses them. This is a small teaching set, not a dictionary.",
    "verifyAt": "https://www.gavo.t.u-tokyo.ac.jp/ojad/ (OJAD, search a reading to confirm its accent)",
    "license": "The accent facts themselves are not copyrightable. This file is released with the repo under MIT.",
    "multiAccentNote": "心 (こころ) is listed here at [2], which Wiktionary attests with DJR and NHK references, but Wiktionary leads with [3]. 卵, 自転車, 頭, 花, 切る and 着る also have more than one attested accent. Where a word has several, this file carries one and does not claim it is the only correct answer."
  },
